{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UfEreLxELv4xB4De4zpArA","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/diytechy/Documents/ai-template-drive/wi-580-the-worker-and-reviewer-briefs/docs/reviews/wi-580-the-worker-and-reviewer-briefs/006-REVIEW-A-69209a9.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed05b759-a83e-44c9-a90c-2decb2e85f3d","uuid":"0f74bd8d-f0cf-49d8-a845-d2fcb903aec7","timestamp":"2026-09-05T04:44:00.172Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/Users/diytechy/Documents/ai-template-drive/wi-580-the-worker-and-reviewer-briefs/docs/reviews/wi-580-the-worker-and-reviewer-briefs/006-REVIEW-A-69209a9.md","oldString":"`pytest tests/test_agent_loop_worker.py tests/test_agent_loop_review.py\ntests/test_module_size_ratchet.py -q` → **`1 failed, 78 passed in 85.93s`**.","newString":"`pytest tests/test_agent_loop_worker.py tests/test_agent_loop_review.py\ntests/test_module_size_ratchet.py -q` → **`1 failed, 78 passed in 85.93s`**.\n\nSecond `check.py` invocation, run only to verify a claim I had put on this\nrecord — the refresh's own shape, `--jobs 0 --tier full --trunk-lane` →\n`RESULT: FAIL (2 step(s) failed)`: `derived-stage` and `verdict-rollup`. Those\ntwo are the generated-freshness gates `--trunk-lane` deliberately forces on and\nthat stand down on a work branch (§5.2) — the trunk lane's business, not this\ndiff's, and NOT raised as findings. What the run was for is the rung list it\nprints, quoted in finding 2.","originalFile":"# WI-580 — REVIEW-A (independent), tip d0654ae1\n\nReading scope: `git diff contract_split...HEAD` minus records/generated. Spec of\nrecord: `docs/archive/work/complete/WI-580-the-worker-and-reviewer-briefs.md`\n(closed cleanly — Deliverable before Context at :13, `specref = \"\"`).\n\n## Worst failure classes this change admits, hunted in order\n\n1. **Silent wrong content in a normative brief** — `assignment_block` /\n   `reviewed_rows_block` inject state into instructions a session obeys. A\n   wrong state word is invisible and consequential.\n2. **Fail-open scope loss** — `{wis}` naming rows a round is not actually\n   reviewing, or the batch block dropping a row.\n3. **Bar erosion** — the new close-bar clause tells workers to run LESS.\n\nFindings 2 and 3 of those were driven and cleared; 1 produced no defect but the\nbar itself is red (BLOCKER below).\n\n## Harness, run here (summaries only)\n\n`python project-trajectory/scripts/check.py --jobs 0` →\n```\nCheck summary (stage DevStg-Tests, tier all):\n  PASS  registry-integrity 5.3s\n  ... PASS trajectory 8.9s / PASS prompt-catalog 0.1s / PASS approval-immutable 0.2s\n  SKIP  derived-stage / approval-fresh / verdict-rollup  (work branch, §5.2)\nRESULT: PASS\n```\n`python project-trajectory/scripts/trace.py --strict-integrity` →\n```\nTraceability: SN=27 SR=76 LLR=191 TC=190 orphans=0 integrity=0 ... paraphrase-advisories=3.\n```\n`pytest tests/test_agent_loop_worker.py tests/test_agent_loop_review.py\ntests/test_module_size_ratchet.py -q` → **`1 failed, 78 passed in 85.93s`**.\n\n## What I drove\n\n- **Review scope is honest.** My candidate MAJOR was `{wis}` listing rows a\n  mid-batch round has not built yet. Killed by reading the real path:\n  `agent_loop.schedule_review_round` (:2838) returns early unless\n  `all(w in built_now for w in worker[\"assigned\"])`, and\n  `review_owed_by_evidence` carries the same precondition. Every row `{wis}`\n  names is built by the time a round is drawn. No finding.\n- **`current_assignment_wi` refactor is behaviour-preserving.** `w not in done`\n  where `done = built - claimed_on_branch` is exactly the prior\n  `w not in built or w in still_open`. Walk order unchanged.\n- **The regression test fails on the pre-fix behaviour** (required check). In a\n  detached scratch worktree at d0654ae1 I replaced `lane_completion`'s two-part\n  answer with the trailer-alone predicate the fix removed and re-ran:\n  `FAILED tests/test_agent_loop_worker.py::test_the_brief_never_calls_an_unclosed_row_built`\n  — `assert '  - WI-204 [started, not closed] …' in \"… - WI-204 [built] …\"`.\n  The test is real, not tautological. Worktree removed; tree clean.\n- **Slot inventory driven, not read**: `string.Formatter().parse` over the\n  worker template body returns **12** names.\n\n## Done-when → coverage\n\n| # | Item | Cover |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | one-turn close bar | `test_worker_brief_names_the_one_turn_close_bar_scratch_and_amendments` |\n| 2 | `{assignment_block}`, states, opening sentence, single-row identity | `test_worker_prompt_single_row_carries_no_assignment_block` + `test_worker_batch_prompt_names_every_assigned_row_and_its_state` |\n| 3 | `{wis}`, override still renders | `test_reviewer_prompt_names_the_rows_under_review` + `…_without_an_assignment_says_so` |\n| 4 | amendment ⇒ regenerate approval brief | covered above; dogfooded — `docs/ratify/CURRENT.md` carries the LLR-061 amendment |\n| 5 | scratch home | covered above |\n| 6 | tests + CATALOG regenerated + **full suite green** | CATALOG green (`prompt-catalog PASS`); **suite NOT green** — finding 1 |\n\n## Findings\n\n- [BLOCKER] tests/test_module_size_ratchet.py:548 -> the committed baseline `\"agent_loop.py\": 2609` is one below the tree: `check_complexity.module_sloc` on a clean tree at HEAD d0654ae1 reads **2610**, so `test_module_sizes_exactly_match_the_committed_baseline` FAILS — and that test collects into the **smoke** tier, i.e. the per-commit bar is red on the very tip under review, which also falsifies Done-when 6 (\"full suite green\"). Commit 69209a90 added the `scripts=scripts_dir(root),` argument to `worker_prompt` (+1 SLOC) and re-derived nothing; the baseline entry's own reason text still accounts only for the earlier `lane_completion` line -> re-derive the baseline to 2610 via the declared `linecounts` generator (`docs/stack.ini [generated]` owns this file) and extend the reviewed-bump reason to name the `{scripts}` line, then re-run `pytest -q -n auto -m smoke` and paste it -> @owner\n- [MAJOR] project-trajectory/prompts/worker.template.md:48 -> the new clause \"You do NOT owe the full unfiltered suite at close\" directly contradicts CLAUDE.md:68 — reached by the same session, since the brief's first instruction is \"Read AGENTS.md first\" and AGENTS.md is a stub pointing at CLAUDE.md — which says to run the full unfiltered suite \"before claiming a WI/slice done, at phase close\". Two authorities over one decision, created by this diff and left unreconciled. The brief's escape hatch (\"the lane's own refresh runs the full declared bar for you\") is also weaker than it reads at this repo's current stage. I re-ran the bar in the refresh's OWN command shape — `integrate._run_bar` issues `check.py --jobs 0 --tier <tier> --trunk-lane` — and its plan carries **no** `format`, `lint` or `tests+coverage` rung at all: `Check summary (stage DevStg-Tests, tier full)` lists fourteen registry/doc/generated steps and not one test step, because the product layer is stage-gated below `DevStg-Impl`. (The commit hook's own plan DOES include `format`, so this is a property of the refresh's shape, not of the repo lacking product steps.) So at today's stage the refresh bar a worker is now told to rely on executes zero tests, while the worker has just been told not to run the suite either -> reconcile in ONE place: either amend CLAUDE.md's self-test bullet to state the same split the brief now states (commit bar in-session, full suite by the refresh / at phase close), or narrow the brief's clause to name the stage at which the refresh bar actually runs the suite -> @owner\n- [MINOR] project-trajectory/prompts/worker.template.md:6 -> \"this prompt is filled from eleven computed values\" is off by one: `string.Formatter().parse` over the body returns 12 slots (`assignment_block base context_block diff_block pred_block rework_block scripts specref srs title train wi`), and the generated `prompts/CATALOG.md` row lists the same 12 — the count word tracked the `{assignment_block}` addition but not `{scripts}`. For clarity: this dispatcher note exists precisely so a maintainer can check the slot set against the fill, and a wrong count is the one thing it must not carry -> change \"eleven\" to \"twelve\" -> @owner\n- [MINOR] docs/archive/work/complete/WI-580-the-worker-and-reviewer-briefs.md:86 -> the WI-559 quote block is headed \"Done-when 1 and 3, verbatim — … item 3 is shared\", but the row's own numbered Done-when pulls only item 1, leaving it unstated whether WI-580 owes item 3's tests (\"drive the false-partial class (built-and-verified lane, long suite) and the adjudicate round scheduling on a scaffold\"). No test in this diff drives the false-partial class, and on the \"shared\" reading none is owed. For clarity, not a defect: the quote block asserts the absorbed Done-when \"remain the spec this row must satisfy\" while the numbered list silently narrows it -> say which row discharges each shared item (e.g. \"item 3 discharged by WI-579\") so a reviewer is not left inferring the split -> @owner\n\n## Note on the antidote clause\n\nNeither remedy above ADDS a check, guard, warn or invariant — finding 1\nre-derives a generated number and findings 2–4 reconcile prose — so no\n\"why not unrepresentable\" clause is owed on those lines. Worth recording for\nthe owner anyway, in the `antidote` skill's terms: the smallest change that\nmakes finding 1 unnecessary is not another detector but the existing one being\n*run* — the baseline is already a declared generated cell, and the smoke bar\nalready fails on disagreement. What failed here was the ritual, not the design,\nwhich is exactly why finding 2's contradiction is worth closing.\n\nVERDICT: CHANGES-REQUESTED findings=4\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":33,"oldLines":6,"newStart":33,"newLines":14,"lines":[" `pytest tests/test_agent_loop_worker.py tests/test_agent_loop_review.py"," tests/test_module_size_ratchet.py -q` → **`1 failed, 78 passed in 85.93s`**."," ","+Second `check.py` invocation, run only to verify a claim I had put on this","+record — the refresh's own shape, `--jobs 0 --tier full --trunk-lane` →","+`RESULT: FAIL (2 step(s) failed)`: `derived-stage` and `verdict-rollup`. Those","+two are the generated-freshness gates `--trunk-lane` deliberately forces on and","+that stand down on a work branch (§5.2) — the trunk lane's business, not this","+diff's, and NOT raised as findings. What the run was for is the rung list it","+prints, quoted in finding 2.","+"," ## What I drove"," "," - **Review scope is honest.** My candidate MAJOR was `{wis}` listing rows a"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
